265
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:09,610
...we work in a museum of natural history.

266
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:12,360
And yet, there is something...

267
00:17:12,610 --> 00:17:14,110
...unnatural...

268
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,110
...about the way we eat lunch.

269
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:22,990
I look around, and you know what I see? I see division.

270
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:28,210
Division between people in white coats and people in blue blazers.

271
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,670
I ask myself, "My God, why?"

272
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,840
Now, I say we shed these coats...

273
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:37,760
...that separate us.

274
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,970
And we get to know the people underneath.

275
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,270
I'm Ross!

276
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:49,770
I'm divorced and I have a kid!

277
00:17:55,990 --> 00:17:58,360
I'm Joey! I'm an actor!

278
00:17:59,110 --> 00:18:01,870
I don't know squat about dinosaurs!

279
00:18:04,450 --> 00:18:09,580
I'm Ted, and I just moved here, and New York really scares me.

280
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:12,750
- There you go!     - Hang in there, Teddy!

281
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:15,510
I'm Andrew.

282
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:18,470
And I didn't pay for this pear.

283
00:18:20,590 --> 00:18:22,390
Okay. Good for you.

284
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:27,430
I'm Rhonda! And these aren't real!

285
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,560
Wow, Rhonda.

286
00:18:35,610 --> 00:18:38,320
- I'm Scott.     - Yeah, okay, Scott!

287
00:18:39,070 --> 00:18:43,570
I flip the light switch on and off 17 times when I leave a room...

288
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,240
...or my family will die.

289
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,120
My mom will be here soon.

290
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,710
I can't. I can't give him up.

291
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,500
Yes, no. I can.

292
00:18:57,130 --> 00:18:58,380
I don't want to.

293
00:18:59,090 --> 00:19:00,470
But I can.

294
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:02,260
No.

295
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:06,560
I can't watch this. It's like Sophie's Choice.

296
00:19:07,850 --> 00:19:09,850
You know, I never saw that.

297
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:12,150
Oh, it was only okay.

298
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,310
I can't do this.

299
00:19:16,070 --> 00:19:19,690
My mom was right. If I can't give him up...

300
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:22,200
...there's no way I can give up a baby.

301
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:26,450
Frank and Alice are going to be so crushed.

302
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:30,290
What else can I give them? A kidney!

303
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,380
We were in the neighborhood.

304
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:40,720
We want to let you know that there's still no pressure.

305
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:41,920
None.

306
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:46,600
If there was something you wanted to say, we'll be right there.

307
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:48,220
Okay.

308
00:19:48,890 --> 00:19:50,430
Who's this little guy?

309
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:53,020
Oh, um, well...

310
00:19:53,850 --> 00:19:57,820
He's so cute! He reminds me of my old dog, Tumor.

311
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:03,360
You are so precious, I'd take you home.

312
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:05,910
Why don't you?

313
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:07,660
Are you serious?

314
00:20:07,870 --> 00:20:08,990
Uh-huh. Yeah.

315
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,950
Thanks.

316
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:17,130
- What are you doing?     - I'm okay with this.

317
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:19,750
You know why? Because look at them.

318
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,800
Look how happy they are.

319
00:20:22,050 --> 00:20:24,930
And I made that, so you know...

320
00:20:27,390 --> 00:20:31,430
...it'll be a million times harder to give up a baby. But God!

321
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:34,390
It'll feel a million times better, right?

322
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:38,860
I'll do this. I want to carry your baby.

323
00:20:39,690 --> 00:20:42,900
Oh!

324
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,490
Thank you so much!

325
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:48,490
You don't know what this means to us.

326
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:52,330
I think I'm going to cry!

327
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:59,750
It's going to be so great.

328
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:01,960
Hi.

329
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,510
- What's going on?     - I gave them the puppy.

330
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:09,600
It made them so happy, I decided to carry their baby.

331
00:21:10,260 --> 00:21:12,180
- Phoebe...     - No, I know.

332
00:21:12,390 --> 00:21:14,060
We're different, though.

333
00:21:14,310 --> 00:21:16,560
This is a different situation.

334
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:19,190
I am not going to regret this.

335
00:21:19,770 --> 00:21:22,280
I understand all that.

336
00:21:22,690 --> 00:21:24,820
It's just, that was my puppy.

337
00:21:24,990 --> 00:21:26,030
Oh!

338
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,990
Would you ever be a surrogate?

339
00:21:33,450 --> 00:21:34,700
Depends who asked.

340
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:36,620
What if I asked?

341
00:21:37,290 --> 00:21:39,460
Oh, Mon, sure!

342
00:21:39,670 --> 00:21:41,920
- Really?     - Yes.

343
00:21:45,670 --> 00:21:47,800
- You're not asking me, are you?     - No.

344
00:21:48,430 --> 00:21:50,180
Yes. Totally.

345
00:21:54,390 --> 00:21:57,060
Thank you! Thank you!

346
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,520
Thank you!

347
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:00,690
Yes, thank you!

